1. hasNext() Method:
hasNext() checks whether there is another element available in the collection or not.
If another element exists → returns true
If no more elements → returns false
👉 Simple meaning:
“Is there a next element?”


2. next() Method:
next() returns the next element from the collection and moves the iterator pointer to the next position.
👉 Simple meaning:
“Give me the next element.”

hasNext() → check
next() → get element
----------------------------------------------------
| Method               | Purpose                       |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `hasNext()`          | Checks if next element exists |
| `next()`             | Returns next element          |
| `remove()`           | Removes current element       |
| `forEachRemaining()` | Processes remaining elements  |
